{"type":"text","timestamp":1794564336624,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba468f8ffe2Nj9hM9jYXmEDS","part":{"id":"prt_1d45ea4e5001FGA4MLfgoeI14S","sessionID":"ses_e2ba468f8ffe2Nj9hM9jYXmEDS","messageID":"msg_1d45e91f2001Cw5SE2vnHzKGe6","type":"text","text":"T011 is done. One sentence replaced in `FC`, verify passed.\n\n**File written**\n\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, line 42. The old sentence `The hook writes records only when \\`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\` is set.` is now `The hook writes a health record on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text only when \\`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\` is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries \\`degraded: true\\`.` Both names stay in backticks, and the surrounding sentences about raw prompts and the 100 ms flush are unchanged.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"writes records only when\" $FC\nexit=1          # no match, prints nothing\n\n$ rg -c \"degraded: true\" $FC\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nBoth conditions hold: the old phrase is gone and the new phrase appears exactly once. `git diff --stat` shows one file, one insertion and one deletion, so no other line moved.\n\n**Not done**\n\nThe `tasks.md` checkbox for T011 is untouched, as instructed. Nothing else was edited.","time":{"start":1794564334821,"end":1794564336624}}}
